  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 301 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nAs the aforementioned trough deepens as it tracks over the \nGreat Lakes into the Ohio valley late Monday into Tuesday, will \nsee a push of cool air advection into Iowa that will end the \nstretch of sweltering heat. While temperatures will only be a \ntouch cooler in the upper 80s to low 90s Tuesday, drier air from\nthis shift in low level flow turning northwesterly will allow \nfor slightly lower dewpoints in the upper 60s for most areas. \nThe western thermal ridge overall will move very little through \nmuch of the work weak, with any precipitation chances signaled \nto largely remain west of Iowa until around Thursday, when a \nmore potent shortwave dives southeast on the eastern fringe of \nthis ridge from the Dakotas into Iowa. Certainly room for slight\nshifts in these larger scale features to occur in the coming \ndays given this being further out in the forecast period, so \nstay tuned for updates. Highs through the rest of the week \nremain generally in the upper 80s to low 90s, paired with \ndewpoints in the 60s, more towards normal summertime averages.",
